Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Cardboard Telescopes Chew the Sun
- Story & Context: When the 1979 solar path cut across the roofs of Bucharest's Bloc 14, Grigore Dan dragged a hollowed-out Czech cello and a rattling diesel rhythm box into the crowd of amateur skywatchers, where the scent of burnt kerosene and melting roof tar hung thick in the midday chill. As two uniformed housing inspectors climbed the fire escape with eviction notices, Grigore drove his horsehair bow across double-stopped C-strings to trigger an intoxicating 122-BPM hustle that froze the officials mid-stride. The roof shook as sixty teenagers in soot-darkened goggles danced on the gravel, transfixed while the band chanted through a copper megaphone, "Count the teeth in the sky while your hips still move."
